From 7dbcae53898c96aaf95e48520daf237d46ba8331 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duck-brain <duck-brain@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:47:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] duck-brain P24: the head's sensors as the duck sees them, in
 the config

Alex's measurement of 08.11.2026, "as the duck sees":
- [tof] rotate (degrees clockwise, 0/90/180/270, default 0): tofd turns
  the sensor's raw 8x8 grid before publishing it, so row 0 is the top
  and column 0 the duck's left - the layout kinematics::tof lays its
  beams out in. The duck's mount is 270. The real sensor only; the
  simulator's and the fake's frames are in that view already.
- [media] rotate (unset follows the board: 90 on the Zero 3W): the angle
  mediad tells every frame consumer, between --rotate and the board.
- Both validated at load; robotctl configure: [tof] restarts tofd.
- robotd body-imu stops on SIGINT as on SIGTERM, also when started with
  SIGINT ignored (in the background, over a non-interactive ssh).
- mediad builds again: robot.say (P7) is refused over a datachannel.
